; The compiler's heap (Shared/Memory/memory_arena.pmi, 32 MB by default on this board) lies in
; the BSS, which this map gives $2000000 up to 1 MB below the stack top at $3000000. Nothing here
; allocates from it: no string is growable (every .s has a room), nothing calls AllocateMemory,
; and the built image holds no allocator - only the arena's reservation. 64 KB keeps that true
; with room to spare; a growable string added later that outgrows it stops the core (the text
; library's pm_text_failed), it does not overwrite anything.
#MEMORY_HEAP_BYTES=65536
; CPU cache ownership belongs to the platform, not video/audio or the NES.
; Match Anvil's WB attributes for resident code/state and secondary mailboxes.
; DMA/framebuffer/GPU arenas stay NC, including every private GPU allocation.
Procedure.i PlatformBegin()
  MmuClearNc()
  MmuAddNc($03E00000,$0D000000)
  If MmuBuildTables($03F00000)<>0 : ProcedureReturn 0 : EndIf
  MmuEnableCached()
  ProcedureReturn 1
EndProcedure
Procedure PlatformEnd()
  MmuDisableCachedFlushed()
EndProcedure
